{{also|höfuð-|hǫfuð}}
==Icelandic==
{{wikipedia|lang=is}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|is|non|hǫfuð}}, from {{der|is|gem-pro|*hafudą}} or {{m|gem-pro|*habudą}}, northern form of {{m|gem-pro|*haubudą}}, from {{der|is|ine-pro|*kauput-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*kaput-||head}}. More at English {{m|en|head}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/hœːvʏθ/}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|n|höfuðs|höfuð}}

# {{lb|is|anatomy}} a [[head]]
#* '''1928''', [[w:is:Krummavísa|Krummavísa]] (“Raven Song”, on the [[w:source:Krummavísa|Icelandic Wikisource]]) by [[w:Jón Ásgeirsson|Jón Ásgeirsson]]
#*: {{quote|is|''Krummi krunkar úti,''<br>''kallar á nafna sinn:''<br>''„Ég fann '''höfuð''' af hrúti''<br>''hrygg og gæruskinn.“''<br>''Komdu nú og kroppaðu með mér,''<br>''krummi nafni minn.''
|translation=“Krummi croaks outside,<br>calling his namesake:<br>‘I found the '''head''' of a ram,<br>backbone and sheepskin.’<br>Come now and peck with me,<br>Krummi, my namesake.”}}
# [[head]], [[chief]]
# the [[ornamental]] [[prow]] of a [[ship]]
#: ''Þetta var skip með gyltum '''höfðum'''.''
# an ornamental head on a [[bridle]]
#: {{ux|is|Slitnaði sundur beislið, og týndist '''höfuðið''', er á var.|The bridle tore and the '''head''' on which it lay was lost.}}

